---
import {getCollection} from 'astro:content'; import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'; import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro'; import GuideCard from '../../components/GuideCard.astro';
const guides=(await getCollection('guides')).sort((a,b)=>a.data.order-b.data.order);
---
<BaseLayout title="5G Home Internet Troubleshooting Guides" description="Diagnose 5G home internet signal, speed, disconnection, gateway placement, and Wi-Fi problems with practical, provider-neutral guides."><Breadcrumbs items={[{name:'Home',href:'/'},{name:'5G Home Internet'}]}/><header class="page-head wrap"><p class="eyebrow">TROUBLESHOOTING HUB</p><h1>5G Home Internet</h1><p class="lede">A clear result starts with the right question: where in the connection does the problem begin?</p></header><section class="section section-tint"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head"><h2>Separate the possible causes</h2><p>Before changing settings, test enough to identify the likely side of the system. Similar symptoms can come from very different places.</p></div><div class="hub-steps"><article><h3>Provider network</h3><p>Outages, maintenance, capacity, or time-of-day congestion upstream.</p></article><article><h3>Cellular & gateway</h3><p>The outdoor-to-indoor radio link, placement, heat, power, or gateway state.</p></article><article><h3>Local Wi-Fi</h3><p>Distance, walls, interference, Wi-Fi bands, or home-network equipment.</p></article><article><h3>Device & app</h3><p>A single device, software setting, VPN, service, or workload.</p></article></div></div></section><section class="section"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head"><p class="eyebrow">STEP-BY-STEP GUIDES</p><h2>Start with your symptom</h2></div><div class="grid-3">{guides.map(g=><GuideCard guide={g}/>)}</div></div></section><section class="section section-tint"><div class="wrap prose"><h2>Use controlled tests</h2><p>Write down the starting condition, change one variable, allow the gateway time to reconnect, and repeat the same test. A wired comparison, when your equipment supports it, can help distinguish an internet-side issue from local Wi-Fi. Keep electrical equipment dry and ventilated, do not defeat safety features, and follow provider and manufacturer directions.</p><p>For a complete five-layer framework, see <a href="/books/the-5g-home-internet-troubleshooting-manual/"><em>The 5G Home Internet Troubleshooting Manual</em></a>.</p></div></section></BaseLayout>
